  "status_text": "Even with NOT gates allowed, a circuit has to look at almost every input wire, and that is now checked for a whole class of graphs at every size. For every n from 2, an AND/OR/NOT circuit of fan-in two representing an n by n graph with pairwise distinct rows and columns has at least 2n - 3 gates [L-meta-19198], checked from outside. It is a floor of reading, just under the 2n inputs; what it adds is breadth: every such graph at once.",
